# Coding Rules

## Single responsibility

Each function does ONE thing. Prefer small, named helpers over long blocks.

## Naming

Use clear names that match domain language: `Signal`, `Event`, `Provider`, `Watchlist`.

```python
# BAD
def do_stuff(x): ...

# GOOD
def cluster_raw_items(items): ...
def passes_quality_gate(signal): ...
```

## No magic values

Thresholds, caps, and source lists belong in `Settings` / constants — not scattered literals.

## Early return

Avoid deep nesting. Validate and return/raise early.

## Comments

Explain WHY (cost, safety, product constraint). Do not narrate WHAT.

## Consistency

Follow existing patterns in `backend/app/` and `mobile/` / `admin/`. Do not invent a new style per file.

## Secrets

Never commit real API keys. Use `backend/.env` (gitignored) and empty placeholders in `.env.example`.
